[E0343] Error: `Maker` cannot be used behind `dyn`
    ╭─[ err/98_dyn_interfaces/main.wip:40:18 ]
    │
 13 │     static fn zero(): Self          // needs the type
    │               ──┬─  
    │                 ╰─── declared here
    │ 
 40 │ fn maker(m: &dyn Maker): i64 = 0
    │                  ──┬──  
    │                    ╰──── `zero` is a `static fn`
    │ 
    │ Help: `Maker` still works as a constraint: `fn f<T: Maker>(x: &T)`
    │ 
    │ Note: a function without a receiver needs the type, which a `&dyn` does not name
────╯
[E0343] Error: `Taker` cannot be used behind `dyn`
    ╭─[ err/98_dyn_interfaces/main.wip:41:18 ]
    │
 17 │     move fn consume(): i64          // needs the size
    │             ───┬───  
    │                ╰───── declared here
    │ 
 41 │ fn taker(t: &dyn Taker): i64 = 0
    │                  ──┬──  
    │                    ╰──── `consume` is a `move fn`
    │ 
    │ Help: `Taker` still works as a constraint: `fn f<T: Taker>(x: &T)`
    │ 
    │ Note: taking the receiver by value needs its size, which a `&dyn` does not know
────╯
[E0343] Error: `Grower` cannot be used behind `dyn`
    ╭─[ err/98_dyn_interfaces/main.wip:42:19 ]
    │
 21 │     fn grown(): Self                // `Self` is not known through a table
